      "descripcion": "Showers and thunderstorms associated with the remnants of Tropical Depression Fifteen-E, located roughly 430 miles south-southeast of South Point, Hawaii, are gradually becoming better organized. Environmental conditions are conducive for development, and a tropical depression is expected to form in a day or so, while the system moves slowly west-northwestward. Heavy rains associated with this system are forecast to spread over the southeastern Hawaiian Islands starting on Wednesday and continuing through Saturday, possibly resulting in life-threatening flash flooding and mudslides for portions of the Big Island and Maui. Interests in the Hawaiian Islands should continue to monitor the progress of this system.",
